.TH JAUGE 1 "2026-08-01" "scheduler" "Zach's utilities"
.SH NAME
jauge \- measure what the ecosystem has spent against what it may
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jauge list
.br
.B jauge burn
.br
.B jauge gate
.br
.B jauge
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jauge
reads how much of the shared quota has been spent and rules on whether more
may be. It is an instrument: it never dispatches anything.
.TP
.B burn
real token and quota burn per project, and the total, read out of the logs
rather than estimated.
.TP
.B gate
the pacing brain's sensor and its verdict \- whether work may start now.
.SS The seam is finer than the domain
The usage domain looks like three scripts.
.B burn
and
.B gate
measure and decide. The third,
.IR usage\-paced\-runner ,
is the pacing
.B dispatcher
\- it acts on that verdict by running jobs. Measuring and dispatching are the
division this family is built on, so the runner stays with
.BR dose (1)
and only the instruments are here.
.PP
A verb that both measures the quota and spends it is the shape this
ecosystem refuses everywhere else.
.SS It wraps, it does not reimplement
Both subcommands exec the existing script in scheduler's own
.IR bin/ ,
unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Not wired for any subcommand of this verb. Requesting it is reported rather
than ignored.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress commentary; results only.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and the exit vocabulary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The promise was kept.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error; the caller is wrong.
.TP
.B 4
GAP: the script a subcommand fronts is absent or not executable, so no
measurement is possible.
.SH EXAMPLES
Listing prints the subcommands, bare, one per line, so a caller reads the
surface without a parser:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ jauge list
list
burn
gate
.fi
.RE
.PP
An unknown subcommand is the caller's error:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ jauge frobnicate
jauge: unknown subcommand: frobnicate  (try: jauge list)
$ echo $?
2
.fi
.RE
.SH COST
Nothing here spends money \- it measures spending rather than causing it. It
offers no
.B \-\-summon
flag for any subcommand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I bin/jauge
This utility.
.TP
.I lib/verb.sh
The shared runtime it sources.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dose (1),
.BR rapporte (1),
.BR relis (1),
.BR arme (1)
.PP
Expectations transfer from
.BR dose (1)
for the domain this verb was cut out of.
.SH HISTORY
Coined 2026-08-01 with
.B bashify coin
as the fifth verb of one noun, completing the split the 2026-07-30 verb
research proposed.
